Loading data from a ``DataSet`` is now faster. Array and complex valued data is read
several times faster since the header of the stored arrays is only parsed once per
parameter rather than once per stored value. Repeated calls to ``get_parameter_data``
on a started ``DataSet``, e.g. when the cache is updated during a measurement, are also
faster as the run description held by the dataset is used rather than reading and
parsing it from the database on every call.
